tandem (4.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The counter said TOTAL 0 and there were seventy-three Portuguese and
    English sentences on screen, in all seven languages. That is the third
    false zero this measure has produced and the second one that shipped. Nine
    were found by reading src/lib/winedeps.sh by hand; a six-lens audit of the
    whole tree then found sixty-four more, in fourteen files.
  * What was on the screen: "Detalhes tecnicos:" under EVERY error window; the
    Sim/Nao buttons of every question that did not pass its own pair; the nine
    component descriptions on the screen where the owner agrees to a half-hour
    download ("Editor de texto rico", "Depurador do Windows", "Desenho de texto
    (Uniscribe)"); the whole of "tandem preparar"; both paragraphs explaining a
    system driver; the headers of the memory file, the recipe and the settings
    file - the three files the product itself invites him to open and send to
    somebody; the column header of the program picker; and the comment written
    into every AppImage menu entry, which outlives the session.
  * The memory values are the largest group and the fix is the one that does
    not break anybody: forty-four values stay on disk exactly as written -
    translating one would break every recipe already sitting on somebody's
    machine - and are resolved to a sentence when they are SHOWN, the same
    arrangement t_erro_do_leitor already uses for the readers' tokens. Until
    now "pasta sem permissao" and "bitola errada" - Brazilian slang no
    dictionary recovers - were what a French owner read on the screen he opens
    to find out what went wrong, and what went into the report he was told to
    send to whoever was helping him.
  * A correctness defect wearing a translation defect's clothes: five handlers
    asked "[y/N]" in English and "[o/N]" in French, from the catalogue, and
    then accepted only s|S|sim|SIM. An English owner did what the screen asked,
    typed y, and was told the install was cancelled. It sat on the .deb and .sh
    paths, the two where the alternative to installing is being told that
    nothing happened.
  * The silent-success guard was arithmetically dead on the runs that matter.
    tandem-exe timed from before the dependency installs, so after a dotnet48
    the elapsed time was half an hour and the "it opened and closed by itself"
    warning - which compares against a few seconds - could not fire. A program
    that flashed and vanished was reported as having worked, and the inflated
    number went into memory and travelled inside recipes.
  * The real change is not the sentences, it is the SECOND INSTRUMENT.
    tools/conta-literais.py reads the source and asks what shape of shell hides
    a sentence; sixteen misses say that question has a floor, and the sixteenth
    proves it cannot be raised by widening - the offending function's name
    matched no prose-body pattern and it lived in a library, so every rule the
    counter has was inapplicable to it. tools/prosa-fora-do-catalogo.py asks a
    different question of a different thing: it RUNS the program and reads what
    comes out. Two angles, because the first has a floor of its own - render in
    Chinese and flag runs of Latin words, and render in all seven and flag any
    line that comes out byte-identical, which is what a literal necessarily
    does and a catalogue lookup almost never does.
  * That tool's own first version did not catch the bug it was written for.
    It wanted three words of three letters and "Editor de texto rico" is
    chopped at "de", so it scored clean - the counter's whole history repeating
    itself inside its replacement, on the first attempt, found only by putting
    the defect back and watching the tool stay silent. A later version then
    invented findings: "sim" on the verbatim list deleted itself out of the
    middle of "simplified". Both are written down where the thresholds are.
  * The three MIME type descriptions carried English plus pt_BR only, so five
    of the seven shipped languages read English in the file manager while every
    .desktop beside that file carried all seven.

